XI-V Bench 1.0
==============

The English base items (32 each for easy/standard/hard, en-*) are excerpted from the
JevBench v1.3 public set (MIT, github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench) and adapted into
the XI-V Bench format. Each item's provenance retains the original id (source_item_id),
the original tier (origin_tier), the license (MIT), and the source attribution.

The Korean, Chinese, and Japanese items are localized adaptations of the English items
above (not literal translations): people, companies, currencies, dates, laws, and
practices were replaced with the context of the relevant locale, while the decision
structure, answer rationale, and trap structure were kept identical to the source.
They correspond 1:1 to the source items via provenance.source_kind="localized" and
provenance.translation_of.

Item label contract: for the noul type, labels are fixed to ["no","yes"] by the harness
contract; these are the probability keys returned by adapters. Localized wording is
preserved inside question.criteria and question.instructions, and the
question.criteria keys must be exactly true/false (the option texts the model reads).
